   "issue": "The descending induction is encoded as `\u2200 n : \u2115, \u2200 q, q + n = b \u2192 \u2026` and entered through `(b - p).toNat`. The base case is closed by two broad `simp_all` calls over a context full of `IsIso` hypotheses. This hides the plain integer induction downward from `b` and makes the base case fragile.",
